---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="Hifz Planner"><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">Make room for revision</span> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Balance new pages with the pages you already know. Adjust your own time estimates and see what fits.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><h2>Your study rhythm</h2> <span class="pill">604-page layout</span></div><form id="plan-form" class="panel-body"><div class="card-grid">
{[['memorized','Pages already memorized',0,0,603,.25],['goal','New pages to add',20,.25,604,.25],['minutes','Minutes per study session',45,1,1440,1],['newMinutes','Minutes to learn one new page',45,1,1440,1],['reviewMinutes','Minutes to review one page',2,.1,120,.1],['pace','Maximum new pages per session',.5,.01,20,.01],['cycle','Review the whole portion every … study sessions',14,1,365,1]].map(([id,label,value,min,max,step])=><><label class="field">{label}<input id={String(id)} name={String(id)} type="number" value={value} min={min} max={max} step={step} required/></label>{' '}</>)}<label class="field">Start date<input id="start" name="start" type="date" required/></label></div><fieldset class="top-gap"><legend>Study days</legend><div class="actions">{['Sun','Mon','Tue','Wed','Thu','Fri','Sat'].map((day,i)=><><label class="pill"><input type="checkbox" name="day" value={i} checked={i>0&&i<6}/> {day}</label>{' '}</>)}</div></fieldset><label class="check-label top-gap"><input id="remember" type="checkbox"/> Remember these assumptions for 30 days</label><p id="error" role="alert"></p><div class="actions"><button class="button">Calculate plan</button> <button class="button secondary" type="button" id="reset">Reset</button></div></form></section> <aside class="sidebar"><div class="notice"><h2>What the model assumes</h2><p>Your memorized pages ÷ review cycle = pages to review each session. New study uses the remaining time.</p><p>Revision is spread evenly. The model does not assess retention, difficulty, recitation accuracy, or teacher guidance.</p><a href="/sources/">Read the methodology ↗</a></div></aside></div><section id="results" class="panel top-gap" aria-live="polite"></section><script>import '../lib/app';</script></Shell>
